{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Has become like one of Us.</b> He is unique among the lower beings as I am unique among the higher beings. And what is his uniqueness? To know good and evil — which is not so in beast and animal." "<b>And now, lest he send his hand.</b> Once he lives forever, he is close to misleading created beings after him, to say that he too is a god. And there are aggadic midrashim, but they do not settle upon the plain sense."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:35.835383601Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}